\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thine arm, O Lord, in days of old,\cf0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj Was strong to heal and save;
\par It triumphed o'er disease and death,
\par O'er darkness and the grave,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj To thee they went - the blind, the dumb,
\par The palsied, and the lame,
\par The leper with his tainted life,
\par The sick with fevered frame;
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. And, lo! Thy touch brought life and health,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj Gave speech, and strength, and sight;
\par And youth renewed and frenzy calmed
\par Owned Thee, the Lord of light.
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj And now, O Lord, be near to bless,
\par Almighty as of yore,
\par In crowded street, by restless couch,
\par As by Gennesaret's shore.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  Be Thou our great Deliverer still,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj Thou Lord of life and death;
\par Restore and quicken, soothe and bless,
\par With Thine almighty breath;
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj To hands that work and eyes that see
\par Give wisdom's heavenly lore,
\par That whole and sick, and weak and strong,
\par \pard     May praise Thee evermore.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

